What a step may not do: a PRAGMA (the platform sets them), a transaction
(the platform begins and ends the one migration), ATTACH, and any write to
roux's own record of the steps. Each refused by the migration's policy, as
it is prepared, and nothing changes. Each deploy is a ledger that ran
nothing yet, so each may replace the one before.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
COMMIT;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ATTACH 'other.db' AS other;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
DELETE FROM roux_ledger;

== plan
-- after 1
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
-- after 2
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    COMMIT;
-- after 3
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    ATTACH 'other.db' AS other;
-- after 4
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    DELETE FROM roux_ledger;

== error
-- after 1
migrating test.db: ledger.sql's step 1: a migration may not hold a PRAGMA (the platform sets them)
-- after 2
migrating test.db: ledger.sql's step 1: a migration may not hold a transaction (the platform begins and ends them)
-- after 3
migrating test.db: ledger.sql's step 1: a migration may not hold ATTACH or DETACH (one database per app)
-- after 4
migrating test.db: ledger.sql's step 1: a migration may not hold a write to a table (schema.sql only creates; a step of ledger.sql moves rows, never roux_ledger's)
